          hints: ['The loop should end when node becomes null, so it runs while node is not null.', 'If the target is smaller than the current value, the answer can only be in the left subtree.', 'The blanks are `node !== null` and `target < node.value`.'],
          explanation: 'The loop keeps walking while there is a node. At each node a single comparison chooses the side that can still hold the target: smaller goes left, otherwise right. Falling off the tree means the value is absent.',
